{
  "requirement": "The `Markdown` implementation of `OutlineLang` supplies the extension, selection, and fingerprint rules described in this chapter.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct Markdown;\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for Markdown;\nimpl Debug for Markdown;\nimpl Default for Markdown;\nimpl OutlineLang for Markdown;\nimpl Copy for Markdown;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.sdk.sources.markdown.Markdown` declares the `Markdown` unit struct and its trait impls (`Clone`, `Debug`, `Default`, `OutlineLang`, `Copy`). It also says the type supplies the extension, selection and fingerprint rules described in the chapter. The detailed rules belong to refining requirements (`requirements.sdk.sources.markdown.language`, `.sections`, `.fingerprints`) with their own tests. They need no separate test here.\n\nMapping to the three reviewed tests:\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` has a generic `check` helper that runs `languages::Markdown` with `a.MARKDOWN` and `# Check\\n`.\n  - Extensions: it asserts `extensions()` equals `[\"md\",\"markdown\"]`, and that every extension, uppercased, infers the language.\n  - Fingerprint scheme: it asserts `fingerprint_scheme()` equals `markdown-structural-v1`.\n  - Selection: it asserts `select(\"section[Check]\")` works and that the outline matches `OutlineLang::outline`.\n  - Trait impls: the `L: OutlineLang + Default + Copy` bound makes `Default` and `Copy` compile-time checks, and the helper calls `L::default()` and `Clone::clone`. It also checks the zero-size layout.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[markdown_heading_levels_resolve_encoded_duplicates_and_anonymous_items]` checks the Markdown selection rules with exact assertions on the section selectors, including encoding, duplicates `#1` and `#2`, nested levels, setext headings, and anonymous preamble and block items. It also checks that selected text and spans are correct.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the SDK public export inventory against rustdoc, and that Habeas compiles against the SDK. This covers the declared public type and its documented surface.\n\nThe only impl not exercised by a behavioural assertion is `Debug`. The text specifies no Debug output, so there is nothing to assert beyond its existence, which the export-inventory test covers. I found no obligation in the text without a test, and no acknowledgments apply.",
